          <div  class="title-page">
               <p>(F) <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">Normal Operation Procedure:</b></p>
              <table cellpadding="2">
                
    <tr>
         <th style="width:6%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th style="width:68%;">Operation Procedure</th>
            <th style="width:11%;">Action by</th>
            <th style="width:10%;">Check</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>1</td>
        <td>
           Inform Control room about commencement of NRO.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>2</td>
        <td>
       Disconnect electric supply and other communication cables to Ultrasonic meter, pressure transmitter, temperature transmitter. </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>3</td>
        <td>
            Remove Pressure transmitter, temperature transmitter and RTD from meter run.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>4</td>
        <td>
       Check for potential sources of ignition in the vicinity of valve H and remove if any.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>5</td>
        <td>
     Install vent stack with flame arrestor at valve H (Size 1/2”) for gas venting purpose and Pressure gauge to monitor pipeline pressure.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>6</td>
        <td>
        Connect hose between vent valve K and vent valve L.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>7</td>
        <td>
      Open vent valves K and L to pressurise meter by pass line.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>8</td>
        <td>
        Gradually open valve G (size 16”) and valve F (size 16”) to start gas flow through meter bypass line. 
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>9</td>
        <td>
		Gradually Close valve A (size 16”) and valve B (size 16”) to isolate USM.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>
		Open valve H (Size 1/2”) and vent the gas in the pipeline till the gauge pressure falls to zero.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>11</td>
        <td>
 	Check the gas % at valve H using gascoseeker and reconfirm zero gas in the pipeline.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>12</td>
        <td>
	Disconnect the meter run from point X and Y and remove the same.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>
      <tr>
            <td>13</td>
            <td>
                Install blind flanges at point X and Y.
            </td>
            <td>
               O&amp;M Technician
            </td>
          <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>14</td>
            <td>
Inform control room about the completion of NRO.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>
</table>
