 <p> <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">(G) Contingency Action Plan:</b></p>
    <p><b style="text-decoration:underline;color:red"> In case of Passing of Valve A (16"):</b> </p>
 <table>	
        <tr>
            <th style="width:10%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th>Description of work</th>
            <th>Responsibility</th>
        </tr>
      <tr><td>1</td><td> Close valve A (16”) completely. </td><td >O&amp;M Technician </td></tr>
     <tr><td>2</td><td> Open needle valve downstream of valve A sealant point. </td><td>O&amp;M Technician </td></tr>
	<tr><td>3</td><td>Connect sealant gun to the needle valve tubing. </td><td>O&amp;M Technician </td></tr>
     <tr><td>4</td><td> Apply sealant using sealant injection gun to ensure passing of valve is completely stopped.</td><td>O&amp;M Technician </td></tr>
     <tr><td>5</td><td>Open valve H (Size 1/2”) and vent the gas in the pipeline till the gauge pressure falls to zero. </td><td>O&amp;M Technician </td></tr>
     <tr><td>6</td><td>Check the gas % at valve H using gascoseeker to ensure zero gas. </td><td>O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
     <tr><td>7</td><td>Disconnect the meter run from point X and Y and remove the same. </td><td>O&amp;M Technician </td></tr>
     <tr><td>8</td><td> Install blind flanges at point X and Y.</td><td>O&amp;M Techcician </td></tr>
     <tr><td>9</td><td> Inform Control Room about completion of NRO.</td><td>O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
     
             </table> 
             
